{title: Christ Receiveth Sinful Men}
{artist: Erdmann Neumeister, tr. Emma F. Bevan / James McGranahan}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{tempo: 65}
{time: 12/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Broadman Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: Broadman Press, 1940), # 113)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Sinners Jesus will receive;
[D]Sound this [A]word of grace to [D]all
[D]Who the heavenly pathway leave,
[D]All who [A7]linger, all who [D]fall.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Sing [G]it o’er [Bm]and over again;__[D]__
[D]Christ receiveth sinful men;
[D]Make [G]the message clear and plain:__[D7]__
[D7]Christ [Em]receiveth sin__[A]__ful__[D]__ men.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Come, and He will give you rest;
[D]Trust Him, [A]for His Word is [D]plain;
[D]He will take the sinfulest;
[D]Christ re[A7]ceiveth sinful [D]men.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Now my heart condemns me not,
[D]Pure be[A]fore the law I [D]stand;
[D]He who cleansed me from all spot,
[D]Satis[A7]fied its last de[D]mand.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Christ receiveth sinful men,
[D]Even [A]me with all my [D]sin;
[D]Purged from every spot and stain,
[D]Heaven with [A7]Him I enter [D]in.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
